 memes that stick  around usually operate well in multiple  modes types of memes existed long before  the internet but the Internet has had a  big influence on memes and the way we  look at them first by increasing the  number of connections and points of  communication it speeds up the evolution  of memes second the internet makes this  evolutionary process much more visible  than it's been in the past before the  internet tracking little-known non image  memes out and culture would have been  extremely difficult although for the  most part memes remain an enigma dick  and difficult to track but maybe it's  worth the effort I think we  underestimate the importance of what a  meme represents the individual meme  might seem trivial but tracking trends  across many memes might reveal the  deeply felt ideas in Internet culture  that they represent maybe we can learn  something about ourselves by tracking  which memes survive at the very least  become an evolutionary force that helps  shape our culture and share a meme  [Music]  building and running a website doesn't  have to be a pain with squarespace's  all-in-one platform and 24/7 support you  can stop fiddling with annoying code and  other details and focus on bringing your  ideas to life although if you do want to  get under the hood and customize things  you can do that too  Squarespace gives you some awesome  templates as a starting place but the  flexible platform lets you customize it  to fit whatever needs you have make your  next move with Squarespace Squarespace  is a one-stop shop to grab a unique  domain and build a beautiful website for  whatever project or idea  you have start your free trial today at  squarespace.com and enter offer code  thomas flight to get 10% off your first  purchase thank you so much to those who  support me on patreon if you appreciate  my content and want to consider  supporting me I hugely appreciate it  it'll help me continue to make these  videos for a long time to come  I'm T